              This should be set to either AAFF__IINNEETT or  AAFF__IINNEETT66  for  IPv4  or
              IPv6 sockets respectively.

       _s_d_i_a_g___p_r_o_t_o_c_o_l
              This  should  be  set to one of IIPPPPRROOTTOO__TTCCPP, IIPPPPRROOTTOO__UUDDPP, or IIPP‐‐
              PPRROOTTOO__UUDDPPLLIITTEE.

       _i_d_i_a_g___e_x_t
              This is a set of flags defining what kind of  extended  informa‐
              tion  to report.  Each requested kind of information is reported
              back as a netlink attribute as described below:

              IINNEETT__DDIIAAGG__TTOOSS
                     The payload associated with  this  attribute  is  a  __u8
                     value which is the TOS of the socket.

              IINNEETT__DDIIAAGG__TTCCLLAASSSS
                     The  payload  associated  with  this  attribute is a __u8
                     value which is the TClass of the  socket.   IPv6  sockets
                     only.   For LISTEN and CLOSE sockets, this is followed by
                     IINNEETT__DDIIAAGG__SSKKVV66OONNLLYY attribute with associated __u8 payload
                     value meaning whether the socket is IPv6‐only or not.

              IINNEETT__DDIIAAGG__MMEEMMIINNFFOO
                     The payload associated with this attribute is represented
                     in the following structure:

                         struct inet_diag_meminfo {
                             __u32 idiag_rmem;
                             __u32 idiag_wmem;
                             __u32 idiag_fmem;
                             __u32 idiag_tmem;
                         };

                     The fields of this structure are as follows:

                     _i_d_i_a_g___r_m_e_m  The amount of data in the receive queue.

                     _i_d_i_a_g___w_m_e_m  The amount of data that is queued by TCP  but
                                 not yet sent.

                     _i_d_i_a_g___f_m_e_m  The amount of memory scheduled for future use
                                 (TCP only).

                     _i_d_i_a_g___t_m_e_m  The amount of data in send queue.

              IINNEETT__DDIIAAGG__SSKKMMEEMMIINNFFOO
